# unit_model_commands_01: unit tests (fx) that start each of the 3D model
# interpreter's commands (render/model.asm) on its own, so its calls can be
# judged; in the game each is reached by its command byte through the
# table at 01:8000 inside FxModelDraw. Each start uses the registers the
# command had at one of its entries in a Novice Coupe race (taken from
# speed_novice_coupe_07/08), from the state of that race whose ROM bank
# register holds the model's bank ($0C or $0E), as the start cannot set it.
# The R10 stack is put back as it was down to the end command's slot
# (01:9243), with the STOP at $01:80E3 in place of FxModelDraw's return,
# so the list runs on to its end and the program stops there; a start
# inside a sub-list's walk (return 01:8E7D) has the walker's table of
# sub-list returns ($0056) emptied, so the walk ends at once. Starts whose
# list then runs on for many frames from the race's RAM are left out;
# FxModelIfSkip has none here. The starts of FxModelPoints01,
# FxModelIfCall, FxModelFramePick and FxModelJump (all but FxModelIfCall
# with registers from the attract_04 and stunt_rockfield_06 plays) also
# empty the draw list ($005C = $08AA), so the program draws only its own
# faces.
load build/stuntracefx/states/speed_novice_coupe_08.state
set 700244 E3,80,43,92
fx 01:8B0E stop=80E3 r10=0248 r0=0820 r1=0500 r2=FB00 r3=0A00 r4=02DC r5=FE73 r6=7BE1 r7=7C2A r8=E121 r9=0364 r12=0000 r13=08FF r14=D9DA
wait 1
load build/stuntracefx/states/speed_novice_coupe_08.state
set 700244 E3,80,43,92
fx 01:8BAA stop=80E3 r10=0248 r0=0D84 r1=F100 r2=0000 r3=0F00 r4=02DC r5=0000 r6=7BE1 r7=7C2A r8=0100 r9=0370 r12=0000 r13=08FF r14=D9DF
wait 1
